<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width">
<title>Your email is being changed</title>
</head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#f4f4f7;font-family:-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#1f2328;">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="background:#f4f4f7;padding:32px 16px;">
<tr><td align="center">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="max-width:520px;background:#ffffff;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #e3e5e8;">
<tr><td style="padding:32px 32px 8px;font-size:20px;font-weight:700;">Your email is being changed</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 32px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;">
<p style="margin:12px 0;">Hi {{.Username}},</p>
<p style="margin:12px 0;">Someone signed in to your account on <strong>{{.InstanceName}}</strong> asked to change its email address to <strong>{{.MaskedEmail}}</strong>. Nothing changes until the link sent to that address is confirmed from a signed-in session; the request expires in {{.ExpiresIn}}.</p>
<p style="margin:12px 0;">If this was you, there is nothing to do. You can also cancel it under Settings &gt; Security.</p>
<p style="margin:12px 0;">If it was not you, reset your password now from the sign-in page (&#34;Forgot your password?&#34;): a reset signs you out everywhere and cancels the change.</p>
</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:16px 32px 28px;font-size:12px;color:#8b949e;">{{.InstanceName}}</td></tr>
</table>
</td></tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
